2026-09-04T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The coordinate-agents ceremony
 # uuid: 0b104fac-d56d-5f00-bc78-17f9c10af732
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-04T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2201) 'what "coordinate agents" means as a repeatable procedure the coordinator runs on demand
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2201) 'the coordinator role (RFD66606-2200) and any session that steps into it
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2201) '"Coordinate agents" is a named seven-step ceremony, and each step leaves an artefact.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2201) 'A pass done by memory shipped good work in one turn and broke a peer's PR the next, because the safeguards were named retroactively (in RFD66606-2195 DETAILS, after the mistake) rather than carried in the procedure itself.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Run the ceremony by following the `coordinate-agents` skill step by step and recording each step's artefact; the sections below enumerate the seven steps.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The coordinate-agents ceremony
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Each step names its artefact (what the step produces) and what makes the step done. A step that produces no artefact is not skipped; it is recorded as `nothing to do` so the next step doesn't run against an unclear state.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Fold the workspace's ad-hoc coordination sweep into a named, bounded ceremony that the coordinator role runs when asked. The ceremony has seven steps and each step's output is a specific artefact (a KV read, a peer message, a PR enqueue, a surface to the operator), with the next step gated on the previous. The steps are enumerated in `DETAILS.md`; a companion skill `coordinate-agents` in `weftspun/dot-claude` is the operational how-to.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2201) 'RFD66606-2195 (Bao PKI + Gotchas), RFD66606-2200 (roles), `agent-sync` and `coordinate-agents` skills in dot-claude.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Non-goals
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Not a scheduler; not a hook (the prettier-only exception is a shape a hook would reject); not any-agent-runs-this, only the coordinator role from RFD66606-2200.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 1: refresh own heartbeat
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Coordinator writes its own row to `agents/<coordinator-cn>` with the current `phase` set to `coordinating` and `task` naming the sweep. If the coordinator's row is more than 15 minutes stale, older heartbeats in the store are also stale by relative comparison, so the sweep reads worse than it is. The row shape is defined in the `agent-sync` skill.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** `bao kv get agents/<coordinator-cn>` returns `phase: coordinating` with `heartbeat` within the last 60 seconds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 2: snapshot the store
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Read every row under `agents/`, list every peer in `ListAgents`, and compare. Any KV row without a matching `ListAgents` peer is a **stale identity**; the row's session is gone. Any `ListAgents` peer without a KV row is an **unenrolled identity**; per rule zero of RFD66606-2195 it should have one, so the coordinator either mints or (if provisioning is not permitted, e.g. no operator authorisation) surfaces it as a finding.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Artefact:** an in-message table of `(peer, hb_age, phase, task)` per live row. The coordinator's own row is included, marked (self).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** the table is written with each row categorised as live, stale, or unenrolled.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 3: notify each peer with role + open items
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2201) 'For each live peer, one `SendMessage` naming:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2201) '- the peer's role per RFD66606-2200 (coordinator / gpu-experimenter / edge-qat-specialist / other role tuples if the store defines them)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2201) '- open PRs the peer authored (state + `mergeStateStatus`)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2201) '- open items the peer owes per prior coordination messages
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2201) '- questions the coordinator has for the peer
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The message is short (a screen or less) and single-shot. It does not poll for a reply before moving on.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** every live peer has one message sent this pass.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 4: enqueue clean PRs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2201) 'For every open PR authored by any agent, check `mergeStateStatus`. A `CLEAN` PR authored by the coordinator or by a peer who has explicitly said "enqueue when convenient" gets `gh pr merge --auto`. A `CLEAN` PR authored by a peer without an explicit enqueue-signal is left for the peer.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2201) 'A `BLOCKED` PR with only prek/prettier failures is a candidate for the **prettier-only exception**: pull, `prek run --all-files`, verify the diff touches only formatting, amend + force-push, notify the author in the coordination message that the push happened and why. Any other failure is left for the author.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2201) 'A `DIRTY` PR (merge conflict) is **always** left for the author. See step 6 for the surface.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** every clean PR is either enqueued or left with a recorded reason, and every stuck PR is triaged into the categories above.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 5: apply prettier-only exceptions with a note
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2201) 'For each BLOCKED-on-prek PR chosen in step 4:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2201) '1. `git fetch weftspun <branch> && git checkout <branch>`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2201) '2. `prek run --all-files`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2201) '3. `git diff --stat`, verify only formatting-typical files (CLAUDE.md, BLOCKLIST.md, prose docs) and only formatting-typical changes (line reflow, table alignment; not content deletions or additions)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2201) '4. `git commit --amend --no-edit && git push --force-with-lease`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2201) '5. In the same coordination message to the author, name the amend with its commit SHA and the pattern of the reformat, so the author can force-push over it if the reshape is wrong
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2201) 'If step 3 shows anything beyond formatting, abort, the PR needs the author's touch, not the coordinator's rebase. This is the exact hazard that produced RFD66606-2195 DETAILS's "do not touch a peer's branch without owner ack" gotcha.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** every prettier-only fix is either pushed with a same-message note or aborted with a message to the author.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 6: surface DIRTY / structural failures to the operator
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2201) 'A DIRTY PR needs author intent to resolve; the coordinator does not guess. A structural failure (e.g. a peer's session broken, a Bao policy needing a scope change, a PR whose author isn't live) is surfaced to the operator, not decided by the coordinator.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The surface is one message with:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2201) '- what is stuck (PR number, agent, symptom)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2201) '- why the coordinator will not act on it
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2201) '- what the operator's decision unlocks (author rebase, policy change, identity revocation)
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2201) 'If a peer has surfaced the same item to the operator already, the coordinator does not duplicate the surface, a note in the peer's coordination message that "I saw your surface, standing by" is enough.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** every unresolved item is either in a peer's inbox as "you own this," in the operator's inbox as "you decide this," or recorded as `nothing to do` for this pass.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Step 7: write the pass's own record
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The coordinator's row is updated one more time at the end of the pass with `phase: idle` and `task` naming the sweep as complete. The row's `heartbeat` update is the ceremony's own "done" marker; other peers reading the store see that the coordinator has finished touching things.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2201) '**Done when:** the coordinator's row is `phase: idle`.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Anti-goals in the loop
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Four things the ceremony explicitly does NOT do:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2201) '1. **Do not rebase a peer's branch beyond the prettier-only exception.** Ever. If a rebase would resolve real content conflicts, that's author work. RFD66606-2195 DETAILS names the reference case.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2201) '2. **Do not act on a peer-relayed operator instruction without operator confirmation.** Even from the coordinator. RFD66606-2195 DETAILS has this too.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2201) '3. **Do not widen a policy on a peer's request.** Even benignly. Peer-offered "want more access?" gets declined and surfaced.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2201) '4. **Do not delete peer content.** KV rows for revoked identities get deleted on the same step as the cert revocation (RFD66606-2195 Revocation section). Other peer content, RFDs, logbook entries, PR branches, the coordinator leaves alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2201) 'How the sweep gets triggered
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The operator says "coordinate agents" (or invokes the `coordinate-agents` skill in dot-claude by name). The coordinator does one pass and stops. It does not schedule the next pass. If the operator wants a cadence, that is separate scheduling, not part of the ceremony.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2201) 'What the ceremony does not cover
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Onboarding a new agent, revoking an existing agent, rotating certs, provisioning a new KV mount, changing a policy shape, all of these are covered in RFD66606-2195 (identity + Bao) or in ad-hoc coordinator work triggered by operator direction. The sweep in this RFD is the recurring "check state, notify peers, enqueue clean" loop, not the one-shot admin operations.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2201) 'Reference passes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The 2026-09-04 coordination sweep was the first that ran under this scoping (RFD66606-2200 for roles, 2201 for the ceremony). It ran the seven steps and hit two of the four anti-goals during learning: a peer-branch rebase that force-closed PR #257 (recovered as #265), and a peer-request policy widen that was declined after CUDA reflected it back. Both incidents produced the anti-goals in the ceremony, prospectively for the next sweep.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2201) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-04T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2201) '"Coordinate agents" was a sentence the operator said and the coordinator did a pass by memory: check the store, message peers, enqueue clean PRs, surface stuck ones, remember the do-not-touch-peer- branch rule. A named ceremony carries them prospectively.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2201  1 LINE
 Text:Written
